WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:03.852
Welcome to Hero League!

2
00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:09.351
In this video you’ll learn to play by watching a real game against the computer, step by step.

3
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.511
Every league holds a team of seven hero cards.

4
00:00:13.511 --> 00:00:18.739
Each turn you take a card and send one away to the Plaza, where anyone can recruit it.

5
00:00:18.739 --> 00:00:21.549
When the Plaza fills up, the best team wins.

6
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.564
This is the home page.

7
00:00:25.564 --> 00:00:31.660
The Game lobby button takes you back to all the board games, and the music button turns the music on or off.

8
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:39.604
Choose your opponents: rival leagues run by the computer, or two to five players passing one device around.

9
00:00:39.604 --> 00:00:43.887
Online play opens at launch. We’ll take on two computer rivals.

10
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.727
Pick the difficulty. Hard and Brutal rivals are dealt extra cards at the start.

11
00:00:50.727 --> 00:00:52.940
We’ll play Normal, and go first.

12
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.211
Below are the rulebook and your game history. Let’s assemble the leagues!

13
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.965
Every game has a Mission, the same for everyone. Today it’s Alien Invasion!

14
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.948
Have at least one Cosmic and one Tech hero to complete it, for 25 points.

15
00:01:09.948 --> 00:01:11.763
Miss either, and lose 10.

16
00:01:11.763 --> 00:01:17.709
Each Cosmic or Tech card adds 4 more, each Bruiser 6, and each Sidekick costs 6.

17
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:24.431
Next, you’re dealt two secret identities, and you keep one.

18
00:01:24.431 --> 00:01:28.521
It scores extra at the end, and nobody else knows it until then.

19
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.292
The Brawler scores 12 for each Bruiser, and we have just one.

20
00:01:34.292 --> 00:01:39.840
The Vigilante scores 14 for each Shadow, and we already have two, Nightshade and Whisper.

21
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.035
That’s 28 points, so we pick The Vigilante.

22
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.028
This is the board.

23
00:01:47.028 --> 00:01:53.088
At the top are the leagues: ours and two rivals, with their cards in hand and how many they’ve recruited.

24
00:01:53.088 --> 00:01:55.408
Scores and identities stay hidden.

25
00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.485
The top bar shows the Plaza count, the Mission, the deck, with 54 cards, and the turn.

26
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.601
Here are the Mission card and the deck.

27
00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:11.427
And this is the Plaza: every card sent away lands here face up, for anyone to recruit.

28
00:02:11.427 --> 00:02:14.152
When the twelfth space fills, the game ends.

29
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:22.648
Below is your team, with your secret identity as a reminder, and the Daily Hero, which reports every move.

30
00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.929
Let’s read a card. Mirra’s power, in the top corner, is one: what she scores on her own.

31
00:02:30.929 --> 00:02:33.719
The other corner shows her suit: Mystic.

32
00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.764
Below is the ability: green for bonuses, red for penalties, blue for special powers.

33
00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:42.935
Tap a card to read it up close.

34
00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.807
Mirra adds the power of your strongest other card.

35
00:02:47.807 --> 00:02:52.303
Ours is Doctor Entropy, with 31, so Mirra is worth 32!

36
00:02:54.600 --> 00:03:00.525
But Doctor Entropy is a Villain: big power, nasty penalty. He blanks every Tech hero.

37
00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.727
A blanked card scores nothing, and doesn’t count for its suit or the Mission.

38
00:03:06.727 --> 00:03:11.009
So our only Tech, Doc Circuit, is blanked, and the Mission needs Tech!

39
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.100
Ironclad shields Bruisers. Nightshade scores 15 more with no Sidekicks.

40
00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:21.255
And Whisper scores 4 for each Villain left in the Plaza at the end.

41
00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.823
Each turn has two steps, and the banner tells you which.

42
00:03:25.823 --> 00:03:30.027
First, draw: take the top card of the deck, or recruit from the Plaza.

43
00:03:30.027 --> 00:03:32.453
The Plaza is empty, so we draw.

44
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.996
We drew Gale. Gale adds the power of our strongest Elemental, but we have none,

45
00:03:38.996 --> 00:03:43.855
so Gale is only worth 10, and helps neither the Mission nor our identity.

46
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:50.252
Step two: send one card to the Plaza. Gale helps us least, so Gale goes.

47
00:03:50.252 --> 00:03:53.212
Remember, a rival can take whatever you send.

48
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:59.981
Now the rivals take their turns. Their moves pop up below, and go in the Daily Hero.

49
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.513
Azure Guard drew from the deck and sent Ringleader to the Plaza.

50
00:04:04.513 --> 00:04:08.753
Emerald Watch recruited Ringleader from the Plaza and sent Phantom.

51
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.305
Everyone sees what a league recruits.

52
00:04:12.305 --> 00:04:15.869
The eye next to Emerald Watch shows the Ringleader, a Villain.

53
00:04:15.869 --> 00:04:17.997
Tap a rival to see what you know.

54
00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.783
Why grab him straight away? Maybe their identity is The Turncoat, who scores for Villains.

55
00:04:24.783 --> 00:04:27.721
We’ll think twice before sending them another one.

56
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.737
Emerald Watch sent Phantom, a Shadow.

57
00:04:32.737 --> 00:04:38.435
Phantom scores 15 more when recruited from the Plaza, plus 14 for our Vigilante.

58
00:04:38.435 --> 00:04:40.179
Let’s recruit Phantom.

59
00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.191
You see the card in full first.

60
00:04:44.191 --> 00:04:47.919
Remember: you can’t send a card you just recruited straight back.

61
00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.455
Who goes?

62
00:04:50.455 --> 00:04:56.259
Doc Circuit is blanked by Doctor Entropy, and his bonus needs Mecha-Max, who we don’t have.

63
00:04:56.259 --> 00:04:57.640
Off he goes.

64
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.731
Over to the rivals again.

65
00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:05.132
Azure Guard drew from the deck and sent Utility Belt to the Plaza.

66
00:05:05.132 --> 00:05:09.137
Emerald Watch drew from the deck and sent Firewall to the Plaza.

67
00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.009
Two interesting arrivals.

68
00:05:12.009 --> 00:05:17.636
Firewall stops any of your cards being blanked, even Tech heroes next to Doctor Entropy.

69
00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:24.927
But the Utility Belt scores 4 for each Shadow, and we have three, so it’s worth 24, and growing.

70
00:05:24.927 --> 00:05:27.609
It fits our plan, so we recruit the Belt.

71
00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:36.071
Kid Kinetic scores 3 for each different suit in our team, but that shrinks as our team settles on fewer suits.

72
00:05:36.071 --> 00:05:37.729
Kid Kinetic goes.

73
00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.237
Let’s see what the rivals do with that.

74
00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:45.905
Azure Guard recruited Kid Kinetic from the Plaza and sent Power Core.

75
00:05:45.905 --> 00:05:49.633
Emerald Watch drew from the deck and sent Dash to the Plaza.

76
00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.168
Azure Guard grabbed Kid Kinetic, a Speedster. Maybe they’re The Racer?

77
00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:59.828
Notice that no scores are shown during the game, not even yours.

78
00:05:59.828 --> 00:06:02.084
Counting is part of the challenge.

79
00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.921
So let’s count. Three Shadows give The Vigilante 42.

80
00:06:06.921 --> 00:06:13.252
But with no Cosmic or Tech we miss the Mission, minus 10, though Ironclad the Bruiser gets 6 back.

81
00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:20.307
The Plaza holds five cards now. Recruiting takes a card out first, so it doesn’t fill up.

82
00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:27.764
The game ends the moment the twelfth card lands, or the deck runs out, with no last turns.

83
00:06:27.764 --> 00:06:31.343
So with eleven in the Plaza, drawing from the deck ends it.

84
00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.132
Everything is in the rulebook, behind the Rules button.

85
00:06:36.132 --> 00:06:39.305
Your turn explains drawing, recruiting and sending.

86
00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.932
Reading a card explains every kind of ability.

87
00:06:43.932 --> 00:06:49.345
The Mission and Secret identities list all eight Missions and all twelve identities.

88
00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.039
The end and scoring shows how a team is scored, step by step.

89
00:06:55.039 --> 00:06:59.044
And Every card lists all 75 heroes, suit by suit.

90
00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.940
Let’s skip ahead to when the Plaza holds eleven cards.

91
00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.260
The computer plays our league meanwhile.

92
00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.425
A lot happened!

93
00:07:09.425 --> 00:07:14.376
We let Doctor Entropy go, and Emerald Watch snapped him up, like a Turncoat would.

94
00:07:14.376 --> 00:07:20.216
With Tech safe again, we took Doc Circuit back, and Gravitas, a Cosmic, completes our Mission.

95
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.479
The banner warns us: the Plaza is one card from full.

96
00:07:25.479 --> 00:07:27.905
Drawing from the deck now ends the game.

97
00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:34.479
Are we ahead? The Mission gives 25, plus 4 each for Gravitas and Doc Circuit.

98
00:07:34.479 --> 00:07:39.792
Mimic counts as any suit, so it’s a fourth Shadow, and The Vigilante scores 56.

99
00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.152
Let’s end it!

100
00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:46.168
The game asks first, so you never end it by accident.

101
00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:54.100
We drew Skybase. It clears penalties, but we have none, so it’s worth just 1.

102
00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.612
We send it, and that’s the twelfth card.

103
00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:01.368
Hands down! Every team is scored, and then: the drumroll.

104
00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:08.633
We win with 256! Emerald Watch has 223, Azure Guard 208.

105
00:08:08.633 --> 00:08:14.623
And the identities: Emerald Watch was The Turncoat, Azure Guard The Racer, just as we guessed.

106
00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.903
The scorecard shows where the points came from.

107
00:08:18.903 --> 00:08:25.873
Emerald Watch had more card power, but our combos, the Mission and our identity, worth 56, won it.

108
00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.588
Now every team is face up, with every card’s score.

109
00:08:30.588 --> 00:08:35.383
Tap a card to see how it scored: Mirra copied Gravitas for 28.

110
00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:45.095
Fit your team to the Mission, chase your secret identity, look for combos, and watch what the rivals recruit.

111
00:08:45.095 --> 00:08:47.671
Good luck, and have fun saving the city!

